{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "Color themes both apps draw from: web (shared/src/themes.ts, CSS variables named --color-<token>) and Android (read from assets by :core ThemePalette). A theme's colors in a mode are neutral[mode] overlaid by the theme's own [mode] tokens, plus avatar-<n>/on-avatar-<n> from avatars[mode] and label-<tone> from labelTones[mode].",
    "labelTone": "labelTone(hex): the Gmail label color's HSL; saturation below 0.15 is gray, else by hue in degrees: <15 red, <40 orange, <70 yellow, <160 green, <195 teal, <255 blue, <290 purple, <345 pink, else red. Unparseable or missing is gray. Cases in shared/testdata/theme-fixtures.json.",
    "avatarIndex": "avatarIndex(email, count): over the lower-cased address's code points, hash = (hash * 31 + codePoint) mod 2^32 starting from 0; the index is hash mod count."
  },
